slug: concussion-return-to-play
title: Concussion in Sport — Recognise, Remove and Return Gradually
area: Sports & Return to Play
level: Foundation
best: 2nd year onwards
minutes: 11
hook: A player takes a knock to the head in a match and says "I'm fine". Is it safe to let them carry on? Concussion is a brain injury that often looks mild but can be dangerous if missed. Learn to recognise it, when to send someone to hospital, and the step-by-step return to play. || Khilari ko match mein sar par chot lagti hai aur woh kehta hai "main theek hoon". Kya usay khelne dena mehfooz hai? Concussion dimagh ki chot hai jo aksar halki lagti hai magar chhoot jaye to khatarnak ho sakti hai. Isay pehchanna, kab hospital bhejna hai, aur khel mein qadam ba qadam wapsi seekhein.
goal: By the end, you'll recognise concussion signs and symptoms, identify red flags that need emergency care, explain why a player must not return the same day, and guide a graded return to learning and to sport. || End tak aap concussion ki alamaat aur nishaniyan pehchanenge, emergency care wale red flags dhoondenge, samjhayenge ke khilari usi din wapas kyun nahi aa sakta, aur parhai aur khel mein darje war wapsi ki rehnumai karenge.

say: **Concussion** is a brain injury caused by a blow to the head or body that shakes the brain. It usually **does not show on a CT or MRI scan**. Signs include being dazed, slow to get up, unsteady, confused or briefly losing consciousness; symptoms include **headache, dizziness, nausea, blurred vision, feeling "foggy"** and sleep or mood changes. The rule is **"if in doubt, sit them out"**: any player with a suspected concussion must stop and **must not return on the same day**. After **24 to 48 hours of relative rest**, light activity that does not make symptoms much worse is encouraged, then a **graded return** step by step. || **Concussion** sar ya jism par chot se hone wali dimagh ki chot hai jo dimagh ko hila deti hai. Yeh aam taur par **CT ya MRI scan mein nazar nahi aati**. Nishaniyon mein madhosh hona, uthne mein der, dagmagana, uljhan ya thori der ke liye hosh khona shamil hain; alamaat mein **sar dard, chakkar, matli, dhundli nazar, "dhund" jaisa mehsoos hona** aur neend ya mood ki tabdeeli shamil hain. Usool hai **"shak ho to bitha dein"**: mashkook concussion wala har khilari ruk jaye aur **usi din wapas na aaye**. **24 se 48 ghante ke nisbatan aaram** ke baad aisi halki activity ki himmat dilayi jati hai jo alamaat ko zyada na barhaye, phir qadam ba qadam **darje war wapsi**.
analogy: A concussed brain is like a **phone with a drained battery after a fall**: it still turns on and looks normal, but it runs out of power quickly when you open too many apps. Return to activity is like **charging slowly** and opening one app at a time, checking it does not overheat. || Concussion wala dimagh **girne ke baad khatam battery wale phone** jaisa hai: yeh ab bhi on hota hai aur normal lagta hai, magar bohat se apps kholne par jaldi band ho jata hai. Activity mein wapsi **aahista charge karna** aur ek waqt mein ek app kholna hai, check karte hue ke garam na ho.
steps: The graded return to sport || Khel mein darje war wapsi
step: Step 1 — symptom-limited activity :: Daily activities that do not provoke symptoms, such as walking at home, after the first 24 to 48 hours. || Qadam 1 — alamaat tak mehdood activity :: Rozmarra kaam jo alamaat na uthayein, maslan ghar mein chalna, pehle 24 se 48 ghante ke baad.
step: Steps 2 to 3 — aerobic, then sport-specific exercise :: Light then moderate aerobic exercise (walking, stationary cycling), then individual running or skill drills without head contact. A mild, brief rise in symptoms is acceptable; stop if they worsen clearly. || Qadam 2 se 3 — aerobic, phir khel ki khaas exercise :: Halki phir darmiyani aerobic exercise (chalna, stationary cycling), phir akele daurna ya skill drills baghair sar ke takraao ke. Alamaat mein halka, thori der ka izafa qabil-e-qabool hai; wazeh barhne par rok dein.
step: Steps 4 to 5 — non-contact then full-contact training :: Harder non-contact training drills, then, only when free of symptoms and after medical clearance, full-contact practice. || Qadam 4 se 5 — non-contact phir full-contact training :: Zyada mushkil non-contact training drills, phir sirf alamaat khatam hone aur medical ijazat ke baad full-contact practice.
step: Step 6 — return to play :: Normal game play. Each step usually takes at least 24 hours, so the full return takes at least about a week, and longer in children and teenagers. Return to school or work comes before full return to sport. || Qadam 6 — khel mein wapsi :: Normal match. Har qadam aam taur par kam az kam 24 ghante leta hai, is liye poori wapsi mein kam az kam takreeban ek hafta lagta hai, aur bachon aur nojawanon mein zyada. School ya kaam par wapsi khel mein poori wapsi se pehle aati hai.

check: A player is briefly dazed after a head clash but says he feels fine after 5 minutes. What should happen? || Sar takrane ke baad khilari thori der madhosh hota hai magar 5 minute baad kehta hai woh theek hai. Kya hona chahiye?
ok: Remove him from play for the rest of the day and assess for concussion || Usay baqi din ke liye khel se nikalein aur concussion ka assessment karein || Yes — if in doubt, sit them out; no same-day return. || Haan — shak ho to bitha dein; usi din wapsi nahi.
no: Let him continue because he feels better || Usay jaari rakhne dein kyunke woh behtar mehsoos karta hai || Symptoms can appear or worsen later. || Alamaat baad mein zahir ya barh sakti hain.
no: Return him after a 15-minute rest if he passes a quick test || Agar woh jaldi wala test pass kare to 15 minute aaram ke baad wapas laayein || A suspected concussion means no same-day return. || Mashkook concussion ka matlab usi din wapsi nahi.
compare: Concussion symptoms or red flags? || Concussion ki alamaat ya red flags?
head: Feature || Khasiyat ;; Usual concussion || Aam concussion ;; Red flag (emergency) || Red flag (emergency)
row: Headache || Sar dard ;; Mild to moderate, eases with rest || Halka se darmiyana, aaram se kam ;; Severe or increasing headache || Shadeed ya barhta sar dard
row: Consciousness || Hosh ;; Brief daze or no loss || Thori madhoshi ya hosh nahi khoya ;; Deteriorating consciousness, seizure || Girta hua hosh, daura
row: Neurology || Neurology ;; Normal strength and sensation || Normal taqat aur ehsaas ;; Weakness, tingling, double vision || Kamzori, jhunjhunahat, double nazar
row: Other || Aur ;; Foggy, tired, light-sensitive || Dhund, thakan, roshni se takleef ;; Repeated vomiting, neck pain, increasing confusion or agitation || Bar bar ulti, gardan dard, barhti uljhan ya bechaini
memory: **Recognise, remove, refer, return gradually.** The four R's keep the player safe from the field to the next match. || **Pehchanein, nikalein, refer karein, aahista wapas laayein.** Chaar baatein khilari ko maidan se agle match tak mehfooz rakhti hain.
mistake: **Strict dark-room rest for weeks.** Long, complete rest is no longer advised: it can prolong symptoms and low mood. After the first 24 to 48 hours, light activity that does not clearly worsen symptoms, and a gradual return to school or work, help recovery. || **Hafton tak sakht andhere kamre ka aaram.** Lamba, mukammal aaram ab tajweez nahi: yeh alamaat aur udasi ko lamba kar sakta hai. Pehle 24 se 48 ghante ke baad halki activity jo alamaat ko wazeh na barhaye, aur school ya kaam par aahista wapsi recovery mein madad deti hai.
check: Which sign after a head injury needs emergency hospital care? || Sar ki chot ke baad kaun si nishani emergency hospital care maangti hai?
ok: Repeated vomiting and a worsening headache || Bar bar ulti aur barhta sar dard || Yes — these can signal bleeding or swelling in the brain. || Haan — yeh dimagh mein bleeding ya sujan ka ishara ho sakte hain.
no: Feeling tired the next evening || Agli shaam thakan mehsoos hona || That is a common, usual symptom. || Yeh aam, mamool ki alamat hai.
no: Mild sensitivity to bright light || Tez roshni se halki takleef || Common in concussion; monitor it. || Concussion mein aam; nazar rakhein.
check: Why must a player never return on the same day after a suspected concussion? || Mashkook concussion ke baad khilari usi din kabhi wapas kyun nahi aana chahiye?
ok: Symptoms can be delayed, and a second blow to a recovering brain can cause serious harm || Alamaat der se aa sakti hain, aur theek hote dimagh par doosri chot sangeen nuqsan kar sakti hai || Yes — that is why the rule has no exceptions. || Haan — isi liye is usool mein koi chhoot nahi.
no: It is only a rule for professional players || Yeh sirf professional khilariyon ka usool hai || It applies to everyone, especially children. || Yeh sab par lagu hota hai, khaas taur par bachon par.
no: A scan the same day always shows the injury || Usi din ka scan hamesha chot dikhata hai || Concussion usually does not show on scans. || Concussion aam taur par scans mein nazar nahi aata.
clinic: **Teach the family what to watch for.** Give written advice on the red flags, ask that someone stays with the player for the first night, and avoid alcohol and driving until symptoms settle. Plan the return to school or work with the teacher or employer: shorter days and screen breaks first, then full days, before any return to contact sport. || **Ghar walon ko sikhayein kis cheez par nazar rakhni hai.** Red flags ka likha hua mashwara dein, kahein ke pehli raat koi khilari ke saath rahe, aur alamaat theek hone tak sharab aur gaari chalane se bachein. School ya kaam par wapsi teacher ya employer ke saath plan karein: pehle chhote din aur screen se waqfa, phir poore din, kisi bhi contact sport mein wapsi se pehle.
reveal: Why are children and teenagers managed more cautiously? || Bachon aur nojawanon ka intezam zyada ehtiyat se kyun kiya jata hai? || The developing brain may take longer to recover, symptoms can last longer, and school learning is easily affected. Guidelines advise return to learning first, a slower graded return to sport, and medical clearance before contact, so their return usually takes longer than an adult's. || Barhta hua dimagh theek hone mein zyada waqt le sakta hai, alamaat lambi chal sakti hain, aur school ki parhai aasani se mutasir hoti hai. Guidelines pehle parhai mein wapsi, khel mein aahista darje war wapsi, aur contact se pehle medical ijazat ka mashwara deti hain, is liye un ki wapsi aam taur par baalighon se lambi hoti hai.
case: A 16-year-old footballer heads the ball awkwardly and clashes with another player. He is dazed, slow to get up and complains of headache and feeling "foggy". He has no vomiting, weakness or neck pain. || He has a suspected concussion without red flags. || Remove him from play, do not allow return that day, give written red-flag advice to his parents, then after 24 to 48 hours start symptom-limited activity, return to school with breaks, and follow the graded return to sport with medical clearance before contact. || His symptoms settle over 10 days; he returns to school in week one and to full matches about 3 weeks after the injury.
safety: **Call an ambulance or go to the emergency department** for loss of consciousness, a seizure, deteriorating consciousness, severe or worsening headache, repeated vomiting, double vision, weakness or tingling in the arms or legs, neck pain or tenderness (protect the neck), or increasing confusion, restlessness or agitation. **Never allow same-day return** after a suspected concussion. || **Ambulance bulayein ya emergency department jayein** hosh khone, daure, girte hue hosh, shadeed ya barhte sar dard, bar bar ulti, double nazar, bazuon ya taangon mein kamzori ya jhunjhunahat, gardan mein dard ya chhoone par dard (gardan ki hifazat karein), ya barhti uljhan, bechaini ya ghusse par. Mashkook concussion ke baad **usi din wapsi ki kabhi ijazat na dein**.
summary: Concussion is a brain injury that usually does not show on scans; "if in doubt, sit them out", with no same-day return. || Concussion dimagh ki chot hai jo aam taur par scans mein nazar nahi aati; "shak ho to bitha dein", usi din wapsi nahi.
summary: Red flags (worsening headache, repeated vomiting, seizure, weakness, neck pain, deteriorating consciousness) need emergency care. || Red flags (barhta sar dard, bar bar ulti, daura, kamzori, gardan dard, girta hosh) ko emergency care chahiye.
summary: After 24 to 48 hours of relative rest, return gradually: symptom-limited activity, aerobic, sport-specific, non-contact, full-contact, then play — school before sport. || 24 se 48 ghante ke nisbatan aaram ke baad aahista wapsi: alamaat tak mehdood activity, aerobic, khel ki khaas, non-contact, full-contact, phir match — khel se pehle school.
card: Can a concussed player return the same day? || Kya concussion wala khilari usi din wapas aa sakta hai? || Never — if in doubt, sit them out. || Kabhi nahi — shak ho to bitha dein.
card: Does concussion show on a CT scan? || Kya concussion CT scan mein nazar aata hai? || Usually not; it is a functional brain injury. || Aam taur par nahi; yeh dimagh ki functional chot hai.
card: How long is each step of the graded return? || Darje war wapsi ka har qadam kitna lamba hai? || Usually at least 24 hours per step. || Aam taur par har qadam kam az kam 24 ghante.
card: Name three concussion red flags. || Concussion ke teen red flags batayein. || Worsening headache, repeated vomiting, seizure (also weakness, neck pain, deteriorating consciousness). || Barhta sar dard, bar bar ulti, daura (aur kamzori, gardan dard, girta hosh).
deeper: Clinic emergencies drill || /learn/clinic-emergencies-drill || The first five minutes when a patient is suddenly unwell. || Mareez ke achanak bigarne par pehle paanch minute.
deeper: Rules every physio should know — Canadian C-Spine || /learn/clinical-rules-canadian-c-spine-nexus-wells || Deciding when a neck injury needs imaging. || Kab gardan ki chot ko imaging chahiye.
source: Patricios JS, Schneider KJ, Dvorak J, et al. Consensus statement on concussion in sport: the 6th International Conference on Concussion in Sport — Amsterdam, October 2022. Br J Sports Med 2023;57(11):695-711. || consensus statement concussion in sport 6th international conference Amsterdam 2022
source: Leddy JJ, Haider MN, Ellis MJ, et al. Early subthreshold aerobic exercise for sport-related concussion: a randomized clinical trial. JAMA Pediatr 2019;173(4):319-325. || early subthreshold aerobic exercise sport-related concussion randomized
source: National Institute for Health and Care Excellence. Head injury: assessment and early management (NG232). London: NICE; 2023. || NICE NG232 head injury assessment early management
